WEBVTT

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.930
Oh, the tropical plant garden, right?
Thanks for your help.

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:45.060
Dad!

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:45.810
Haruka!

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:48.690
Haruka!

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.190
What's the matter, Haruka?

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:55.110
On second thought,
I'm too old for that stuff now.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.780
Haruka...

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.620
This is how a date should be.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.000
Stop acting so grown-up!

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.710
What about you? You got hit on!

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:07.540
Huh? You saw that?

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:08.920
I sure did.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.920
That was nothing.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.420
She was just asking me
about places to sightsee.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.470
Hmm... She sure was pretty.

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:16.510
Y-You think so?

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.840
Yeah.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.240
You're sure you're okay
coming to a place like this?

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.280
Yeah. I like it here.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:04.200
I feel kind of relieved that you're
still happy with amusement parks.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:07.580
Dad, do you remember?

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:08.830
Huh?

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:10.000
See that?

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.750
When I was still in Tokyo...

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.800
do you remember when we all went
to Grandma's house for summer break?

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.470
Oh, yeah. You still remember that?

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:23.340
We all stayed over at Grandma's house
where I live now.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.180
Yeah, we did.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:29.520
We all came to this
amusement park together.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.190
It sure was fun...

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.780
Do you still resent me?

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.070
What?

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.040
Not at all, dad!

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:53.370
I... was just reminiscing
about fun times.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.420
Hey, Dad?

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:57.040
What's up?

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:01.630
Do you think this place will
still be here when I grow up?

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.140
Haruka, have you started
seeing ghosts again?

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:08.890
Ghosts?

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:12.640
When you were little, you cried a lot
saying you saw ghosts, remember?

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:16.610
Oh, that. Turns out
they weren't ghosts.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:27.280
Hello?

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.950
Hey there, Mayuzumi-chan.
I've been looking for you.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:33.580
You should tell me
when you change cell phones.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.580
Didn't I say we should discuss it
one more time in detail?

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.420
You're with your daughter
right now, aren't you?

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:43.550
You haven't seen her in a while, right?
Enjoy it while you can.

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:47.890
It's not uncommon for
twelve year old girls like her...

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:50.350
to get hit by cars, you know?

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:54.890
You must worry... as a father
without parental authority.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.360
Very well. When should we meet?

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.150
Where?

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.200
All right, in two hours then.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.410
Haruka, I'm afraid I have...

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.410
Work?

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:15.870
Yeah... I have to return
to the hotel right away.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.750
That's all right. Go on...

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:18.500
What?

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:19.920
Get going.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:20.880
Hey...

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:24.380
Instead, I'm going to Tokyo
to see you next time.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:25.420
Tokyo?

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.390
I can go there by myself!
It's just Tokyo.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:31.220
You can spoil me double then!

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.930
Hey, don't push so hard.

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:36.230
Move it, move it!

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.630
What did you make your dad
buy for you this time?

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.970
Actually, he got this call from work...

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.800
...and he had to leave right away.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.810
What?! Even though he came
all this way to see his daughter?

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:15.390
Yeah, that's the thing.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:18.390
Geez, that's unbelievable!
Next time you see him...

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:21.230
you gotta make him buy you extra stuff
to make up for this visit.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:22.900
Absolutely!

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.610
Haruka...

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:28.700
Haruka, Tobi is gone.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:30.530
What? Tobi's gone?

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.620
Maybe he's gone out for a walk?

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.410
Karasu isn't here either.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:41.000
Atori, don't look so sad.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.710
Have some of these!

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:44.960
Thanks, Miho.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:52.720
Aw, you're getting the crumbs
all over the place.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:54.720
It's all over your mouth too.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:58.730
I think Miho's taken a liking to Atori.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.520
I think it is coming from here.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:07.030
A dimensional strain is showing, Karasu.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.530
Karasu?

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:11.990
What is it, Tobi?

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.490
Karasu, is something wrong?

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.490
No...

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.250
Back when we were kids...

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:23.540
we believed that time invariably
moved from the past to the future.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:28.420
Yeah. We all didn't know
any better back then.

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:33.800
But the concept of time isn't
just a measure conceived by man.

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:38.350
We learned that it is merely a fluctuating
value, which is linked with space.

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:41.520
Karasu...

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:47.940
When we learned that both time
and space are always changing without stability...

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:51.200
perhaps mankind lost sight
of the meaning of existence?

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.410
This dimension, La'cryma...

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.790
Both myself, and Haruka...

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.750
Maybe we were all an illusion.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:04.750
You're wrong about that.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:09.760
Our existence is established
by observation.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:13.930
You found Haruka.
That's why she exists.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:17.260
And Haruka found you.

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:21.560
That's why you're here.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.730
What do you hope to achieve
by driving around the mountain?

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:33.610
I'm going to put the strain of
quantum potential into numerical value.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:36.240
Do you think doing that
will persuade those guys?

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:39.740
I don't think it will work
at the committee meeting, but...

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:43.040
...I'm sure someone like
Dr. Mayuzumi will understand.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:46.580
Still, you don't know where
that professor is, right?

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:50.250
I'm sure that he will go to Haruka-chan...

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:57.640
What's wrong?

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:58.220
It's them.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.520
Kooriyama-san?

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.060
You stay here!

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.230
Hey! Kooriyama-san?!

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:07.650
Hey, you!

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:11.650
What are you doing over there?

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:13.490
Karasu!

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:19.280
I'm a cop. I want to
ask you a few questions.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.490
Kooriyama-san!

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:27.040
C'mon, you can speak
my language, can't you?

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.460
Come over here!

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:33.130
I told you to get your butt over here!

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:36.680
Why, you!

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:43.140
Oh, come on... No parlor tricks!

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:49.650
Why are you wearing such a thick cape
on a blistering hot day like today?

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:52.150
Who the hell are you?

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.990
It's pointless to ask.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:57.110
It's way over your head.

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:01.120
Forget and leave this place.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:04.330
I don't THINK so.
I'm not on a child's errand.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:06.830
I want a full explanation.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:10.580
Who are you? What are you doing here?

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:13.710
In ten years.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:18.760
When ten years' time has
passed in this dimension...

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:21.260
I'm sure you will be able
to comprehend my existence.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:24.720
Who do you think you are,
some sort of prophet?

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:27.560
I'd like to talk with you
more at lengths...

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.690
...like in a room with
iron-barred windows!

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:32.610
Wait a second! Tell me...

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:35.690
Are you a transported existence from
a time-space several years ahead?

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:42.370
Is it a world where
the solution of relativity between quantum mechanical application
and space-time has been identified?

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:46.580
I think that explanation will be
too difficult for Karasu to follow.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:50.080
But you're on the right track.
You're brilliant, lady.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:54.290
You might be able to comprehend us.

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:58.510
Who the hell are you guys?

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:02.510
Hey, Isami?

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.720
Yeah, what?

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.600
I really do think it's bad.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:07.470
What's bad?

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:12.690
It's about Haruka.
I think she has strange powers.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:14.770
What brought that on suddenly?

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:17.820
Saying she's got strange powers,
don't start talking like Mukai!

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:21.280
Yeah, but Karasu keeps
telling me to protect her.

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:24.830
Well, we ARE men!

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:27.200
It's our job to keep the women safe!

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:29.080
Yeah. So...

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:30.790
Do you like any girl in particular?

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:33.960
Of... Of course I do!

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.670
What kind of guy would I be
if I didn't like a girl or two?

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:39.170
Wow, so you do like someone. Who is it?

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:40.970
Okay. This is top secret, Yuu.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.340
Yeah.

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:44.760
Miss Yukie?!

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:47.680
I... Idiot! You're impossible!
Keep your voice down!

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:50.180
Everyone knows that.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:54.190
Th-That's impossible! How did word get out?

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:57.190
I was a fool to ask you.

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:59.820
What do you mean, Yuu?!
I'm serious about her!

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.150
Yeah, yeah.

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:06.280
What's this? More trickery?

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.450
This area is definitely suspicious.

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:11.830
Is there a site of wavering here?

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:13.170
Probably.

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:16.960
It's coming from in there.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:19.960
I'm getting a reading
from that area, Karasu.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:21.800
Let's go.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.220
What do you mean, let's go?

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:24.680
Let's go.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:26.680
Hey! Uchida-chan...

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:28.970
Oh, brother.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:38.480
What?! Aw, I sprang a leak again.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:40.690
I'm out of wrenches.

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.660
Dammit... Okay, take this!

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:49.450
I don't think so, Ai! It will
take more than that measly trick to disrupt MY water supply!

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:52.370
Argh! She got my pipe again!

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:54.210
You're good at this, Miho.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.540
Nobody can defeat me!

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.460
It's a trap!

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.260
Ai, you suck.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:07.510
What's the matter, Atori?

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:11.350
It's them.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:12.470
Huh?

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:20.150
I confirmed the reading over here.

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:22.780
But it's a very weak reading...

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:26.530
That's it all right.
It's making a small critical reaction.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:30.580
Hey, what's there?

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:32.160
Karasu, come here a second.

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:34.870
Is this it?

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:38.080
An irregular oscillation
is manifesting inside.

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:39.960
What can you see?

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:42.250
Straight ahead, right?

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:42.920
Yeah.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:52.390
I don't see anything.

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:54.140
It's not visible to the untrained eye.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.150
It's at the critical stage all right.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.780
Critical stage?

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:06.490
What is that?!

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:12.990
What is that ring-like thing?

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:15.250
That is the dimensional contact point.

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:19.210
The Uroboros.

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:23.750
An Uroboros...

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:25.460
Hey, Uchida-chan, be careful!

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:29.430
Don't, Uchida-chan!

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:33.060
Your hand passed through it.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:34.600
Tobi-kun, is this...?

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.480
That is not defined as an existence.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:38.060
What?

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:40.150
Speaking at your scientific level...

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:44.150
it is a quantum existence.
It's in an overlapped state.

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:48.570
Something that can't be defined
as an existence? Not that again!

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:51.490
So even though that ring is
visible to me, it's an illusion?

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:54.410
Or am I just going insane?
Well, which is it?!

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:02.880
See ya, Haruka.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:05.750
Bye-bye! Atori, thanks for
walking them home!

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:07.840
I'll be back soon, Haruka.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.300
See you tomorrow!

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:24.360
What're you doing, Haruka?

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:25.650
Huh?

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:27.610
Put down a card already.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.820
She's spacing out again.

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:37.830
Hey, what's wrong?

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:39.120
Tobi-kun?!

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:42.330
This undulation... Is it Shangri-la?!

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:43.790
Shangri-la?

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:47.050
It's him. The mask of Shangri-la!

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:49.760
Mask?

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:52.510
Karasu, it's Haruka. She's in danger!

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:03.350
Argh, there's no more water works cards!

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:06.020
Haruka, you gotta stop her!

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:11.860
Give it up! My victory
is still guaranteed!

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:26.040
Wha... What is this?

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:28.040
Get out of my way!

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:01.700
Karasu!

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:13.970
Come here, Haruka.

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:26.900
Stand back, Haruka!

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:27.940
Karasu?

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:30.360
Come here, Haruka...

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:32.940
Come to me.

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:36.450
No... You aren't Karasu.

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:38.450
Who are you?!

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:41.990
Come here, Haruka...

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:54.460
The man in the mask?

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:06.810
Haruka, come with me to Shangri-la.

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:10.690
Haruka, watch out!

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:21.700
Haruka!

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:29.170
What's wrong, Yuu?

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:30.080
It's Haruka...

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:30.670
Huh?

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:32.460
Haruka's been kidnapped!

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:46.390
This place...

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:47.890
This is the ravine.

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:50.190
The dimensional ravine.

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:53.650
Haruka, get behind me.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:55.190
Karasu...

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:56.610
Stay close to me!

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:58.150
Haruka...

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:01.660
Come here. Come to me.

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:13.130
That man...

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:16.000
I am Noein...

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:19.220
...the one who understands all.

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:21.220
Now, come with me...

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:26.430
Haruka, come with me to Shangri-la.

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:27.930
Shangri-la?

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:30.940
Yes, the ideal dimension.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.230
I... don't want to go!

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:47.740
Karasu?

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.710
Where is this place?

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:59.170
This is Shangri-la, Haruka.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.590
There is neither war nor pain here.

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:04.760
It is a world veiled in silence.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:08.310
This world is perfection.

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:15.190
Right now, the world is trying to merge into this ideal dimension.

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:17.190
Integrating?

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.730
Yes, Haruka.

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:22.950
Dimensions where you exist...

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:25.660
Dimensions where you do not exist...

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:31.000
All the different dimensions were
branching off into a disorderly mess.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:33.580
Into a literal chaos.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:37.000
Infinite dimensions...

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:40.420
...equal infinite misfortunes.

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:46.180
That is why I forced
the dimensions to conjoin.

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:50.850
Into La'cryma and Shangri-la.

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:56.600
Which of them will you choose?

00:20:57.190 --> 00:21:00.480
Me? Choose?

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:06.870
Haruka!

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:08.870
Haruka!

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:10.580
Karasu!

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:15.210
Get back, Haruka!

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:16.330
Karasu!

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:33.520
You scum!

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:35.600
Disappear!

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:54.200
Haruka...

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:56.210
Why, Haruka?

00:21:56.660 --> 00:21:58.250
Haruka...

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:02.750
Karasu!

00:22:02.750 --> 00:22:05.090
You can forget about him.

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:09.220
Since he is an illusion to you...

00:22:09.470 --> 00:22:12.350
You're wrong! Karasu isn't an illusion!

00:22:12.350 --> 00:22:14.470
My Karasu is right here!

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:15.730
What's this?

00:22:26.440 --> 00:22:29.990
You killed Fukuro...
You killed Isami, didn't you?

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:32.580
I will never believe you!

00:22:34.240 --> 00:22:35.950
The Uroboros.

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:52.180
Hey, Yuu! What's the rush! Yuu!

00:22:52.970 --> 00:22:54.930
What's going on?

00:23:03.690 --> 00:23:05.190
Karasu.

00:23:06.320 --> 00:23:08.190
Where's Haruka?!

00:24:42.250 --> 00:24:45.250
I'm dreaming again.

00:24:45.250 --> 00:24:47.090
That summer day's dream.

00:24:48.460 --> 00:24:51.380
Where is Haruka?!
What happened to Haruka?!

00:24:55.220 --> 00:24:57.390
I get the feeling
it's slightly different.

00:25:02.060 --> 00:25:03.390
Do you want to know?

00:25:04.270 --> 00:25:06.560
Next episode: Repeat.

00:25:07.610 --> 00:25:10.400
Will I be able to meet you again?
